course: dictionary
lesson: 12701
title: Doe and the deer family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A doe is a female deer. Read the words around it to check. «The doe and her fawn walked slowly through the forest.» A fawn is a baby deer, so the doe must be the mother.
explain: Clues can also tell you which animal is meant. «Maya counted three bucks and two does in the field.» The bucks are the males, so the does must be the females. Try swapping in «female deer» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Doe is used for some other female animals too, such as rabbits, hares, goats and kangaroos. When you read about one of these, the other words in the sentence tell you which animal it is.
fact: A doe is a female deer.
fact: Females of rabbits, hares, goats and kangaroos are also called does.
fact: The male deer is a buck or stag, and the baby deer is a fawn.
fact: One doe, two does: the plural of doe is does.
fact: Careful: «does» is also the verb do, as in «What does she want?»
exercise: «The doe and her fawn walked slowly through the forest.» What is a doe? | *A female deer | A male deer | A kind of tree | A baby deer
exercise: «Maya counted three bucks and two does in the field.» What are the bucks? | The male deer | The baby deer | The trees | *The female deer
exercise: Which word means a baby deer? | does | doe | *fawn | buck
test: In a maths lesson, the teacher says, «There are four bucks, three does and two fawns.» How many deer are there altogether? | *9 | 4 | 7 | 5
test: In the story, «The doe lifted her head and listened.» Which animal is listening? | A fox | A male deer | *A female deer | A baby deer
exam: Which sentence uses «does» as the plural of doe? | Tom does not like rain | *Ben saw three does grazing in the field | Ben does his homework every night | What does the fawn need?
